Venetium 0042 - GPU YUV->RGB for software-decoded video (VP9/AV1/software H.264) on ANGLE D3D9 (BATCH MEDIA-1).
Without GL_EXT_texture_rg every software frame was converted YUV->RGB on the CPU and uploaded as a 4-byte RGB texture. Chromium 77
used LUMINANCE_8 planes instead. Now: 8-bit single-channel planes (I420/I422/I444) are uploaded as GL_LUMINANCE (native D3DFMT_L8)
on ANGLE D3D9 (GL_ALPHA elsewhere without texture_rg) and converted in the GPU shader. Service: UseLuminanceForSingleChannelPlanes()
drives BOTH GLFormatCaps::GetFallbackFormatIfNotSupported and GetMultiPlaneFormatInfo so viz/Skia and the backing agree;
CopySharedImageHelper::WritePixelsYUV retypes kR8_unorm pixmaps to the backend channel. Client: WritePixelsYUV and
VideoResourceUpdater accept single-channel 8-bit planes without texture_rg; 2-channel UV (NV12) stays on the CPU path; the kill
switch is --disable-features=VenetiumSoftwareVideoGpuYuv. Contexts with texture_rg and non-D3D9 ANGLE are unchanged.

